# Optional yt-dlp cookies file — placeholder only, contains NO real cookies.
#
# You only need this if YouTube bot-blocks your server's IP and yt-dlp
# reports "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" (LOGIN_REQUIRED).
#
# How to create the real file:
#   1. In a desktop browser where you are signed in to YouTube, install a
#      "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" style extension.
#   2. Export cookies for youtube.com in Netscape format.
#   3. Save the export as cookies.txt IN THIS FOLDER (next to this file),
#      i.e. config/cookies.txt — it is git-ignored and mounted into the
#      container at /config/cookies.txt.
#   4. Restart the container/server. The server passes it to yt-dlp via
#      --cookies (YT_DLP_COOKIES env var) only when the file exists.
#
# Treat cookies.txt like a password: it is a live YouTube login session.
# Never commit it, never share it.
